        "notes": "round 5 is  [Triage Unit](item_fec0554c-2685-4b93-822d-bf0020e654b4)'s time to shine.\n\nthis is also the time to start collecting the staples for this build.  [Amari's Antidote](item_67e0b1c5-3bcb-4ab5-b818-5082e5706124),  [Booster Jets](item_a291de85-b6d9-43cf-b5da-f3184a156f48) and  [Commander's Clip](item_ff7cad01-2065-4908-a2c1-3bdf1458c7a4) are very essential for this round and the rest.\n\nhowever, ammo capacity will only matter if you can afford to dps more often than usual. so it's okay to get rid of  [Commander's Clip](item_ff7cad01-2065-4908-a2c1-3bdf1458c7a4) if you need to and switch it for something else. we're typically only pulling out our gun during Valkyrie or if we're fighting for our life one-on-one. and since Valkyrie gives infinite ammo... well, you see where i'm going. i'd recommend   [Volskaya Ordnance](item_396c0970-daa8-47e3-8049-e65f03fe5cec) in its place.\n\nnot to boast, but i'm pretty good at utilizing Guardian Angel without cooldown reductions. but if it's one of those games where an enemy (looking at you Reaper/Moira and sometimes Freja (\u14c0_\u14c0)) are just every which way i go, and can't get away quick enough, i will buy and stick with  [Icy Coolant](item_8b1c21e9-33e8-49a6-8277-a3a06d55a65f) for however long is needed just to be a bit quicker on my escape. OR if my team is doing excellent, i'll buy  [Angelic Acrobatics](item_baad85fc-3da5-43af-ad9d-f17885f59aa5) simply for the maneuverability. even if it means giving up attack speed. not ideal, but sometimes you gotta do whatcha gotta do.",
